{%- comment -%}
  Renders Google reviews synced into metaobjects by the sync-google-reviews Claude skill.

  The cards come from snippets/mionas-review-card.liquid -- the same snippet the hand-configured
  blocks/mionas-review-card.liquid renders -- so a Google review and a hand-entered testimonial are
  the same component with different data behind them.

  Why a section and not a block: a block is one card, and the carousel treats each block as one
  slide, so a block that looped would put every review inside a single slide. A section can own both
  the row and the summary line beneath it, which is also why no separate container section is needed
  to place the summary.

  Why day-of-year rotation and not random: Shopify full-page-caches storefront pages for anonymous
  visitors and Liquid has no random filter, so a per-request pick would be frozen into cached HTML
  and served identically to everyone anyway. Seeding from the day rotates the selection daily, stays
  cache-friendly, needs no JavaScript, and leaves the reviews visible to search engines.

  Why a stride instead of a contiguous window: picking offset, offset+1, offset+2, ... always shows
  entries adjacent in creation order, so on any given day the cards look clustered from a similar
  period rather than sampled from the whole pool. Picking every Nth entry instead (offset + i*stride)
  spreads the selection across the full enabled pool. For every pick to land on a distinct entry,
  stride must be coprime with enabled_count -- if it shares a common factor, the sequence of picks
  cycles back on itself before reaching show_count distinct values and the same review renders twice.
  enabled_count varies at runtime (reviews get added/disabled), so the stride is computed below rather
  than hardcoded: start near enabled_count / show_count (spreads picks evenly across the pool) and
  walk forward until a coprime value is found, via a bounded Euclidean-algorithm gcd check, falling
  back to 1 (a plain contiguous window) if nothing else qualifies.

  metaobjects.<type>.values loops a maximum of 50 entries, oldest-created-first -- this is Shopify
  Liquid's platform ceiling and cannot be changed. The sync skill's transform.jq caps each RUN at 25
  reviews, a separate and much smaller curation cap chosen to leave headroom below the 50-entry
  ceiling; that per-run cap is not cumulative -- the skill is create-only and never trims, so stored
  entries accumulate across runs and anything past slot 50 (the platform ceiling) is invisible here.
  Keeping the total at 50 or fewer is an operator task done in the Shopify admin, not something this
  section or the skill enforces. Switching a review's enabled field off does NOT free a slot: the
  filter below runs after Liquid has already truncated to 50. See the "Housekeeping" section of
  .claude/skills/sync-google-reviews/SKILL.md.

  Display order is metaobject creation order, NOT newest-first. Entries carry created_at, but nothing
  sorts on it -- deliberately. Liquid cannot sort out of the 50-entry truncation, which happens before
  any sort or filter could run, so sorting here would reorder an already-wrong window. The rotation
  below therefore walks entries in creation order.

  No structured data is emitted here on purpose: Google's structured-data policy excludes
  self-serving aggregate ratings gathered from another platform.

  Every colour comes from existing --review-card-* and --link-* tokens; this section introduces no
  new token and touches neither assets/design-tokens.css nor ../design-system.
{%- endcomment -%}

{% liquid
  assign pool = metaobjects.google_review.values
  assign summary = metaobjects.google_review_summary.default

  # A review with no enabled value predates the field and is treated as enabled, so entries
  # created before this field existed keep rendering.
  assign enabled_count = 0
  for review in pool
    if review.enabled.value == false
      continue
    endif
    assign enabled_count = enabled_count | plus: 1
  endfor
%}

{%- if enabled_count > 0 -%}
  <div class="mionas-google-reviews">
    {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}
      <h2 class="mionas-google-reviews__heading">{{ section.settings.heading }}</h2>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- liquid
      assign day_of_year = 'now' | date: '%j' | plus: 0
      assign offset = day_of_year | modulo: enabled_count
      assign show_count = section.settings.review_count
      if enabled_count < show_count
        assign show_count = enabled_count
      endif

      # Approximate stride: spread show_count picks evenly across enabled_count entries. Force
      # float division (divided_by truncates when both operands are integers) and round to the
      # nearest whole stride -- truncating instead would bias small pools toward stride 1, which
      # is just the old contiguous window in disguise.
      assign stride = enabled_count | times: 1.0 | divided_by: show_count | round
      if stride < 1
        assign stride = 1
      endif

      # Walk forward from the approximate stride until gcd(candidate, enabled_count) == 1.
      # The (0..enabled_count) range covers every residue mod enabled_count at least once, so a
      # coprime candidate is always found when enabled_count > 1 (candidate == 1 is always coprime).
      assign found_stride = 0
      for i in (0..enabled_count)
        assign candidate = stride | plus: i
        assign candidate = candidate | modulo: enabled_count
        # candidate 0 is never coprime with enabled_count (unless enabled_count is 1, handled by
        # the fallback below), so skip it rather than let a false gcd of enabled_count through.
        if candidate == 0
          continue
        endif

        assign gcd_a = candidate
        assign gcd_b = enabled_count
        for j in (0..enabled_count)
          if gcd_b == 0
            break
          endif
          assign gcd_remainder = gcd_a | modulo: gcd_b
          assign gcd_a = gcd_b
          assign gcd_b = gcd_remainder
        endfor

        if gcd_a == 1
          assign found_stride = candidate
          break
        endif
      endfor

      if found_stride == 0
        assign found_stride = 1
      endif
      assign stride = found_stride

      assign show_count_minus_1 = show_count | minus: 1
    -%}

    <div class="mionas-google-reviews__grid">
      {%- assign enabled_index = -1 -%}
      {%- for review in pool -%}
        {%- if review.enabled.value == false -%}
          {%- continue -%}
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- assign enabled_index = enabled_index | plus: 1 -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign selected = false
          for i in (0..show_count_minus_1)
            assign pick = i | times: stride
            assign pick = pick | plus: offset
            assign pick = pick | modulo: enabled_count
            if pick == enabled_index
              assign selected = true
              break
            endif
          endfor
        -%}
        {%- if selected -%}
          {% render 'mionas-review-card',
            rating: review.rating.value,
            quote: review.comment.value,
            name: review.author.value
          %}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>

    {%- if summary != blank -%}
      {%- liquid
        assign score = summary.average_rating.value | round: 1 | append: '' | replace: '.', ','
        assign profile_url = section.settings.profile_url | default: summary.profile_url.value
      -%}
      <p class="mionas-google-reviews__summary">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true" class="mionas-google-reviews__star">
          <path d="M10 1.6l2.47 5.34 5.87.58-4.38 4.05 1.24 5.76L10 14.6l-5.2 2.73 1.24-5.76-4.38-4.05 5.87-.58L10 1.6z" />
        </svg>
        <span class="mionas-google-reviews__score">{{ score }}</span>
        <span class="mionas-google-reviews__separator" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
        <span>{{ summary.total_count.value }} {{ section.settings.reviews_label }}</span>
        {%- if profile_url != blank and section.settings.link_label != blank -%}
          <a class="mionas-google-reviews__link" href="{{ profile_url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            {{- section.settings.link_label -}}
          </a>
        {%- endif -%}
      </p>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{% stylesheet %}
  .mionas-google-reviews {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .mionas-google-reviews__grid {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: row;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-md);
    justify-content: center;
  }

  .mionas-google-reviews__summary {
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: row;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: var(--space-xs);
    font-family: var(--font-body--family);
    font-size: var(--text-role-caption-font-size);
    line-height: var(--text-role-caption-line-height);
    font-weight: var(--text-role-caption-font-weight);
    letter-spacing: var(--text-role-caption-letter-spacing);
    color: var(--review-card-attribution-foreground);
  }

  /* One star beside a number, not five: the average is fractional, and a five-star row would need
     partial-fill clipping the card never had to solve. */
  .mionas-google-reviews__star {
    width: var(--review-card-rating-icon-size);
    height: var(--review-card-rating-icon-size);
    fill: var(--review-card-rating-filled-color);
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .mionas-google-reviews__score {
    color: var(--review-card-quote-foreground);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-bold);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  .mionas-google-reviews__separator {
    color: var(--review-card-rating-empty-color);
  }

  .mionas-google-reviews__link {
    color: var(--link-base-foreground);
    font-weight: var(--link-base-font-weight);
    font-size: var(--link-size-sm-font-size);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .mionas-google-reviews__link:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Mionas: Google reviews",
  "disabled_on": {
    "groups": ["header", "footer"]
  },
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "Heading",
      "info": "Optional. Leave blank to show only the cards."
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "review_count",
      "label": "Reviews shown",
      "min": 3,
      "max": 5,
      "step": 1,
      "default": 5,
      "info": "Which reviews appear rotates daily."
    },
    {
      "type": "url",
      "id": "profile_url",
      "label": "Google profile link",
      "info": "Optional. Falls back to the link stored by the last sync."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "reviews_label",
      "label": "Reviews label",
      "default": "reseñas en Google",
      "info": "Shown after the review count. Plain text on purpose — rebuilding Google's wordmark in another typeface breaks their brand guidelines."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "link_label",
      "label": "Link label",
      "default": "Verlas todas",
      "info": "Optional. Leave blank to hide the link."
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Mionas: Google reviews",
      "category": "t:categories.basic"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
